/*
 * The ke1xz lptmr0 clocks the prescaler from a 128 kHz source and bypasses it,
 * so the 16-bit counter wraps at 0.512 s -- less than the 2 s the sysmanaged
 * layer forces. Divide by 8 instead: 16 kHz puts the range at 4.096 s, and one
 * tick at 62.5 us is still finer than the 140 us exit latency the node declares,
 * so the forced transition is timed by a single alarm rather than chopped into
 * re-armed pieces.
 */
&lptmr0 {
	/delete-property/ prescale-glitch-filter-bypass;
	prescale-glitch-filter = <2>;
};
